integ5 0075 = patches/glue5/0070-glm-shared-window-segment-launches.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.
integ5 resolution: cuda_latent.zig keeps attn5 0068's fuses/fused before attentionSegs. cuda_state.zig partial_rows takes both rules: prompt buffers attn5 0068's (nch x part_rows, sparse prompt calls past them fuse), shared decode buffers this patch's (part_chunks x rows), other decode buffers the old max; .part_chunks and attn5's .partials.rows as each patch sets them.

glm cuda: a shared window's per-stream KDA chains and latent attention in one launch each (T3 candidate 5, glue5)

A shared verify window (several streams' rows in one forward) ran each segment's KDA chain and latent attention as
separate launches, one stream after another: tiny grids, latency-bound (prof5's 4-stream forward: 2.34 ms of them
against 0.72 ms for a lone forward). Now each layer's kernels take every segment at once:
- glm_kda.cu: tf_glm_kda_prep_segs / _step_segs / _out_segs (KdaSegs by value, z: the segment) call the existing
  prep/step/out bodies with the segment's rows, states, saves and conv window; each segment's q and y scratch rows
  sit at its own offset of the window's scratch (cuda_shared stops reusing them segment after segment).
- glm_glue_attn.cuh: tf_glm_chunks_16_fp8_paged_segs / tf_glm_merge_segs (AttnSegs by value: x the window's rows,
  each block finds its segment; z the most chunks, blocks past their segment's chunks leave). chunks_wide takes the
  row and chunk explicitly (defaults: blockIdx, the six existing chunk kernels' SASS unchanged); the merge's body is
  copied word for word for the batched kernel (tf_glm_merge itself untouched).
- cuda_shared.mixer: decode windows on the three-kernel KDA chain take kda.chainSegs; their DSA layers take
  dsa_block.attendWrite + (sparse) attendSelect per segment, then one latent.attentionSegs, when every segment is
  E4M3 on pages, fits one dense block, and is wholly dense or wholly sparse (all of one kind); otherwise the old loop.
  dsa_block.attend is attendWrite + the old attention (same launches, same order). TF_GLM_SHARED_SEGS=0 (read once
  at load, local to the rank: no collectives) keeps the per-segment launches.
- cuda_state: a shared decode buffer holds every segment's attention partials apart: part_chunks (max of the dense
  pass's and a sparse pass's chunks) x its rows: +6.3 MiB a rank on the 32-row shared buffer at TP2.
- Exact: each block runs its segment's own launch's code on the same data: outputs byte for byte against the
  per-segment launches (glue5/bench_kdasegs.cu: saves, states, out rows; glue5/bench_attnsegs.cu: dense and sparse
  out rows), and the SASS of every existing glm_kda and glm_glue kernel is unchanged.

